<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archduke Rainer Joseph of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1783">1783</a>–<a href="/years/1853">1853</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Archduke Rainer Joseph was a son of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany">Leopold II</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. He served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</a> from 1818 to 1848, residing mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, and presided over its efficient but unpopular administration until the revolutions of 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria.jpg" alt="Archduke Rainer Joseph of Austria" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luigi Pedrazzi? um 1840-1850 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erzherzog_Rainer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
